Step 13 — Real OpenFlow Port Statistics
Objective

Right now our congestion module understands utilization if we give it numbers manually:

$$ Utilization = \frac{Used\ Bandwidth}{Link\ Capacity} $$

But we don't want manually supplied numbers.

Ryu should ask the OpenFlow switches:

How many bytes and packets have passed through each port?

From two measurements we calculate actual traffic rate:

$$ Rate=\frac{Bytes_{new}-Bytes_{old}}{Time_{new}-Time_{old}} $$

This will eventually feed our cost:

$$ Cost=w_1(Latency)+w_2(Jitter)+w_3(Loss)+w_4(Utilization) $$

Today, Step 13 only collects real port statistics and calculates traffic rate.

